{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release critique","packet_sha256":"1055e807b96731f32ef34faa63fa4372b098224e838fa6d0671f8483dbc08b44","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"8ed15a89282efc8496eac49882e4ef386718b7115f0742d6a068b3276b047acf","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"release-evidence-incomplete","severity":"blocking","summary":"The bound receipts do not establish the declared release verification surface.","evidence":["The packet declares documentation, secrets, Python lint, code-length, scan-hygiene, subprocess-form, shell, packaging validation, adapter, workflow, and standing-pytest checks as owning-surface validators.","The verification receipt records only packaging sync as clean, one JS mutation dry-run, an earlier full JS mutation run, and 227 tests across 11 focused targets.","No bound result is supplied for the remaining declared validators, and focused targets are not evidence that the full standing pytest gate passed."],"action":"Run or bind receipts for every applicable declared owning-surface validator, explicitly disposition any inapplicable command, and regenerate the final-head verification receipt."},{"id":"full-mutation-not-final-head-bound","severity":"blocking","summary":"The full Stryker result is explicitly stale-by-contract for release approval.","evidence":["The receipt labels the full run as an earlier run and says to rerun it at release time after any tree change.","Only the dry-run is stated to be bound to head e61e13959.","The reviewed identity also includes two untracked evidence files, so the abbreviated Git head alone does not bind the complete reviewed input identity."],"action":"Rerun the required full mutation proof after the release content is frozen and bind its result to the exact reviewed-input identity or an equivalent complete content manifest."},{"id":"delegation-claim-unproven","severity":"high","summary":"The lane probe proves root workspace writing and trust-warning absence, but not the reader-facing claim that delegation remains available.","evidence":["docs/agent-task-runs.md states that trusting the worktree means delegation stays available.","The probe records only that \"Agent delegation: auto unavailable\" was absent from stderr; absence of that message is not a delegation roundtrip.","The probe's performed behavior was git status plus creation and commit of probe-871.txt."],"action":"Either add a bounded delegation exercise/readback to the lane probe or narrow the documentation and evidence claim to what was actually observed."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The Muse workspace-root fix itself may still be invalid.","bin":"not-a-blocker-on-current-evidence","disposition":"The command construction, focused tests, and live lane write/commit probe consistently support the single trusted worktree workspace behavior."},{"concern":"The earlier full Stryker result had six surviving mutants.","bin":"not-inherently-blocking","disposition":"The reported score is above the configured 80 threshold and has zero NoCoverage mutants; the problem is final-content binding, not the survivor count."},{"concern":"No Goal Run lineage is present.","bin":"not-applicable","disposition":"The packet explicitly records not-goal-bound critique lineage; this does not substitute for or invalidate release evidence."}],"next_move":"Freeze the release content, run and bind the complete applicable release gate set—including a final-content full Stryker run—and either prove delegation behavior or narrow that claim before requesting another bounded review.","non_claims":["This review does not claim the current workspace differs from the inline payload.","This review does not reject the Muse workspace-root implementation itself.","This review does not treat unbound or partial verification progress as release approval."]}
